      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\), we first need to find the distances \\(XY\\), \\(YZ\\), and \\(ZX\\). Points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively. This means that \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) are the midpoints of the sides of an equilateral triangle \\(ABC\\) with side length 12.\n\nWe start by calculating the distance from \\(X\\) to \\(Y\\). Since \\(X\\) and \\(Y\\) are midpoints of \\(AC\\) and \\(BC\\) respectively, the line segment \\(XY\\) is a midsegment of the triangle \\(ABC\\). The length of a midsegment in an equilateral triangle is equal to half the length of the side of the triangle. Therefore, the distance \\(XY\\) is:\n\\[\nXY = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the distance from \\(Y\\) to \\(Z\\). Since \\(Y\\) and \\(Z\\) are midpoints of \\(BC\\) and \\(DC\\) respectively, the line segment \\(YZ\\) is also a midsegment of the triangle \\(ABC\\). Therefore, the distance \\(YZ\\) is:\n\\[\nYZ = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6\n\\]\n\nFinally, we calculate the distance from \\(Z\\) to \\(X\\). Since \\(Z\\) and \\(X\\) are midpoints of \\(DC\\) and \\(AC\\) respectively, the line segment \\(ZX\\) is also a midsegment of the triangle \\(ABC\\). Therefore, the distance \\(ZX\\) is:\n\\[\nZX = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 12 = 6\n\\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of the lengths of its sides:\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = XY + YZ + ZX = 6 + 6 + 6 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
